Package: os7-desktop-theme
Version: @OS7_VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Bastian Wirth <bastian.wirth@upinblue.com>
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Depends: dconf-cli, dconf-gsettings-backend, libglib2.0-bin, gnome-shell-extension-user-theme, gnome-shell-extension-window-list, gnome-shell-extension-apps-menu, gnome-shell-extension-places-menu, gnome-shell-extension-launch-new-instance, fontconfig
Homepage: https://github.com/upinblue/os7
Description: OS/7 Classic — the Windows 2000 desktop surface for GNOME
 A GTK 3 theme, a GNOME Shell theme, a set of libadwaita colour overrides and
 the desktop defaults that select them, giving OS/7's GUI mode the look a
 Windows administrator already knows: the "Windows Standard" palette, square
 bevelled controls, a caption gradient, a taskbar along the bottom edge and a
 black desktop.
 .
 It is built only from parts Ubuntu itself keeps in step with GNOME — the
 Classic session extensions from GNOME's own gnome-shell-extensions source
 package — plus this package's own files, and it overwrites no file belonging
 to another package. That is what lets it survive a distribution upgrade
 instead of being reapplied after every one.
 .
 GTK 4 / libadwaita applications receive the classic COLOURS only. libadwaita
 ignores widget themes by design and no supported mechanism exists to give
 them classic shapes; see /usr/share/doc/os7-desktop-theme/README.md.
